         <div style="padding:10px; line-height:30px;">
         <b>Title:</b>  <a href='http://www.vvchem.com/products/search_Hydramethylnon-p1.html'>Hydramethylnon</a><br/><b>CAS Registry Number:</b>  <a href='http://www.vvchem.com/cas-674/67485-29-4.html'>67485-29-4</a><br/><b>CAS Name:</b>  Tetrahydro-5,5-dimethyl-2(1<i>H</i>)-pyrimidinone[3-[4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]-1-[2-[4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl]ethenyl]-2-propenylidene]hydrazone<br/><b>Synonyms:</b>  1,5-bis(a,a,a-trifluoro-<i>p-</i>tolyl)-1,4-pentadiene-3-one (1,4,5,6-tetrahydro-5,5-dimethyl-2-pyrimidinyl)hydrazone<br/><b>Manufacturers' Codes:</b>  AC-217300<br/><b>Trademarks:</b>  Amdro (BASF);  Combat;  Maxforce<br/><b>Molecular Formula:</b>  C25H24F6N4<br/><b>Molecular Weight:</b>  494.48<br/><b>Percent Composition:</b>  C 60.72%, H 4.89%, F 23.05%, N 11.33%<br/><b>Literature References:</b>  Slow-activating stomach poison insecticide.  Prepn:  J. B. Lovell, <b>US</b> <b>4087525</b> (1975 to Am. Cyanamid).  Activity:  <i>idem,</i> <i>Proc. Br. Crop Prot. Conf. - Pests Dis.</i> <b>1979,</b> 575.  Field trials for control of red imported fire ant:  D. P. Harlan <i>et al.,</i> <i>Southwest. Entomol.</i> <b>6,</b> 150 (1981); W. A. Banks <i>et al.,</i> <i>ibid.</i> 158; for control of cockroaches:  J. F. Milio <i>et al.,</i> <i>J. Econ. Entomol.</i> <b>79,</b> 1280 (1986).<br/><b>Properties:</b>  Crystals from isopropanol, mp 189-191°.  Insol in water.  Sol in alc, acetone.<br/><b>Melting point:</b>  mp 189-191°<br/><b>Use:</b>  Insecticide. 
